{
  "title": "Web: shared async-action and resource-loading primitives \
(loading/error boilerplate repeated ~30x)",
  "description": "Two flavors of the same missing abstraction in ramekin-ui:\n\
\n\
1. The skeleton `setXLoading(true); setError(null); try {...} catch { \
setError(...) } finally { setXLoading(false) }` is hand-rolled ~30 times \
across mutating handlers, e.g. pages/ViewRecipePage.tsx:410-443, 519-536, \
pages/EditRecipePage.tsx:88-101, pages/ShoppingListPage.tsx (multiple, per \
catch list at 58-143), pages/TagsPage.tsx:48-213. Add a createAsyncAction \
primitive that wraps a promise and exposes { run, loading, error }; adopt \
incrementally.\n\
\n\
2. Nearly every page re-declares `const [loading] = createSignal(true); const \
[error] = createSignal(null)` plus an onMount/createEffect fetch for initial \
load — TagsPage.tsx:23-24, ShoppingListPage.tsx:15-16, EditRecipePage.tsx:20, \
MealPlanPage.tsx:58-59, ViewRecipePage.tsx:132-133 — where Solid's \
createResource already covers it. Provide a createApiResource wrapper \
standardizing loading/error and adopt per page.\n\
\n\
While adopting, route all catches through extractApiError(err, fallback) so \
real server errors stop being discarded for hardcoded strings (fail-fast).\n\
\n\
Web-only infrastructure; no iOS counterpart needed (its equivalent is the \
view-model extraction issues).",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 3,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "web",
  ],
